      "mergeID": "62f609677ae27144ad9b4136",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Version:w_2020.2.1p1\nDescription of the bug:The stereoscopic images taken by the panoramic camera are the same, and they do not look stereoscopic.\nThe photo I took at the beginning of March was able to take a stereoscopic view because I was able to take it with the right and left eye cameras.\nパノラマカメラで撮影した立体視画像が同じものであり、立体的に見えない。\n三月のはじめに撮影した写真は右目のカメラと左目のカメラで撮影できていて、立体視ができた。",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Panorama camera is not stereoscopic",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e894eb5d87cbd0b05f34e1e",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I second this report. I miss being able to take true stereo 360 photos like you used to be able to do. Also, related and mentioned elsewhere - the panorama now shows avatar body parts of the picture taker, where it used to automatically remove the picture takers avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
